onsistent — Lirien explicitly briefed her in ch12 (lines 130-156). (3) The resonance bond transmits emotions/sensations only, never thoughts or factual information — ch13 explicitly states 'it did not transmit words' (line 66) and 'transmitting not information but intensity' (line 206). (4) Kaelith does not reference Warden lineage through Ossya Thenndal (unknown to her). (5) Kaelith does not reference the contract loophole (unknown to her).\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"magicSystemCompliance\\\": {\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"pass\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Resonance bond mechanics fully consistent with MAG-007. Bond transmits: agitation, grief, attention quality, concern, emotional state, physical sensations, presence. Bond does NOT transmit: words, thoughts, factual information. The recursive feedback loop during the kiss (sensation doubled and returned) is emotional/sensory amplification, consistent with rules. Kaelith's returned magic sensing Pallor erosion is reasonable for a recovering Tier 2 mage detecting a world-scale environmental phenomenon.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"calwrathDetails\\\": {\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"pass\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"All Calwrath details verified against character profile and continuity tracker. Matches: 8 minutes to decide, eastern defensive line, Canal District embankments, Graymarket, 3000 residents, evacuation incomplete, military-grade accelerant, Shaper Tarris (female, served 2 years with Kaelith), fire arrives everywhere at once (90 seconds), plaster dust/pine resin/rendered fat smell, pressurized hissing sound, temple collapse, 312 confirmed dead, 47 children under 12, rank stripped, Oathbranded, permanent exile, official finding: excessive force. Six years consistently referenced throughout (9 instances).\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"namingConsistency\\\": {\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"pass\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"All names verified: Kaelith, Lirien, Calwrath, Tarris, Graymarket (one word), Canal District, Ashborne Legion (not Ashbourne), Vael'thrin (with apostrophe), Elisi, Oathbrand, Pallor, Ythara, Quietus, Tessen (confirmed in ch11), Thalen Reyvas, Seep. No spelling deviations detected.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"romanceArcProgression\\\": {\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"pass\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Chapter delivers the 'First Kiss — Witness Without Flinching' beat per the romance arc. Vulnerability ladder step matches (sharing the unforgivable parts). Emotional throughline matches: trust offered as deliberate risk (Kaelith), witness as intimacy (Lirien). Kiss explicitly framed as choice, not necessity or bond-compulsion — satisfies TP-3 (chosen vs only). The kiss is earned through mutual confession, consistent with the arc design.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"crossChapterDiscrepancy\\\": {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"DISC-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"major\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"flagged_not_fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Thalen Reyvas is assigned the Sixth Seat (Fae Relations and Border Diplomacy) in world-bible/politics.json. However, chapters 10, 12, and 13 all consistently refer to him as holding the Seventh Seat. The Seventh Seat in politics.json belongs to Vairen Ethis (Archives and Knowledge Stewardship). NOT fixed in ch13 because: (a) all drafted chapters are internally consistent with 'Seventh Seat', and (b) changing ch13 alone would create inconsistency with ch10 and ch12. Requires global resolution — either update politics.json to assign Reyvas the Seventh Seat, or update chapters 10/12/13 to use Sixth Seat.\\\",\\n      \\\"affectedArtifacts\\\": [\\n        \\\"world-bible/politics.json\\\",\\n        \\\"chapters/010/draft.md\\\",\\n        \\\"chapters/012/draft.md\\\",\\n        \\\"chapters/013/draft.md\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Since three drafted chapters consistently use 'Seventh Seat' and zero use 'Sixth Seat' for Reyvas, the most efficient resolution is to update politics.json to swap Reyvas to the