        "reasoning_text": "Now I have everything I need. Let me write the status.json and prepend to manifest.json. Let me create the agents/craft-enforcer directory first, then write the status, then update the manifest.\n\nMy assessment is:\n- 15/16 PASS, 1/16 PARTIAL (T23), 0/16 FAIL\n- No edits needed to draft.md\n- Overall craft score: 9/10\n- Pass rate: 93.75% (15/16)\n\nWait, let me reconsider whether T23 is truly PARTIAL or just a note. The chapter correctly closes MB-006 and doesn't open inappropriate boxes. \n\nActually, the 12 active count is a craft-level concern — the tool's mandate is to keep readers driven by 2-3 active questions, and 12 is well beyond that threshold even accounting for foregrounded questions. I should mark it PARTIAL. And looking back at T12, the craft-profile requires both arcs to advance or create pressure on each other, but SCN-35 is purely romance with the fantasy arc completely absent — that's another PARTIAL.\n\nWait, though — the bond does function as a fantasy mechanism enabling the confession, and the chapter's romance deepening creates vulnerability that will amplify the black moment's consequences in chapter 16. The chapter outline was designed this way intentionally, and T12's \"at minimum\" clause is satisfied by that pressure dynamic. I'll keep T12 as PASS with a note.\n\nNow I need to check whether the voice maintainer's corrections actually made it into the current draft — specifically that passage around line 202 about the space between them compressing.\n\nBoth corrections are there: the convergence language at line 202 and the \"bond cracked open\" phrasing at line 222. Good.\n\nTime to write up the status and manifest.",
