        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "id": "tooluse_d5INXyMfJDafx0CDSwc5P4",
            "type": "function",
            "function": {
              "name": "create",
              "arguments": "{\"path\": \"/home/jakubs/repositories/books/romantasy-book-1/.romantic-fantasy-writer/stories/001/agents/craft-enforcer/status.json\", \"file_text\": \"{\\n  \\\"agent\\\": \\\"craft-enforcer\\\",\\n  \\\"chapter\\\": 13,\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n  \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-03-18T07:45:00.000000+00:00\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Chapter 13 craft enforcement audit completed. Systematic scene-by-scene and tool-by-tool verification of all 16 active craft tools against 3 scenes (SCN-34, SCN-35, SCN-36). 15 of 16 tools PASS, 1 PARTIAL (T23 Mystery Box Inventory — chapter-level behavior correct but aggregate active count of 12 exceeds 3-7 target range; this is a plotting-level structural concern, not a chapter-drafting deficiency). Zero FAIL grades. No corrections applied to draft.md — the chapter is craft-compliant as written. The Calwrath confession and first kiss are executed with exceptional craft discipline: subtext layers are rich and consistent, voice fingerprinting is unmistakably Kaelith, all three thematic pillars are dramatized through action rather than stated, foreshadowing payoff FS-007 delivers as planned, symbolic motifs appear at appropriate density with evolution, and the emotional throughline progresses cleanly from defensive fear to courageous vulnerability. Second-pass paragraph-level audit found no MRU ordering violations, no micro-tension dead spots, and no significant show-don't-tell lapses.\\\",\\n  \\\"overallCraftScore\\\": 9,\\n  \\\"fixesApplied\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"passRate\\\": \\\"93.75%\\\",\\n  \\\"craftToolCompliance\\\": {\\n    \\\"T5_toneContract\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-34\\\", \\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"SCN-34\\\": \\\"Morally complex and atmospherically taut. Camp setup under pursuit threat. Dry wit: 'You're building a windbreak that will not break wind.' No prohibited tones detected — no whimsy, no melodrama, no grimdark nihilism. Emotionally restrained: Kaelith's agitation shown through displacement activity (building the windbreak) rather than stated.\\\",\\n        \\\"SCN-35\\\": \\\"Confession delivered in operational briefing register — clinical flatness containing devastating content. 'She told it like a briefing. Because that was how she survived things.' Emotion leaks through restraint, not through declaration. Avoids melodrama despite dealing with war crimes — the prose trusts the content to carry the weight. Forbidden tone 'sentimental/melodramatic' actively resisted throughout.\\\",\\n        \\\"SCN-36\\\": \\\"Darkly romantic register for the kiss — 'not gentle, not desperate' avoids genre sentimentality. Heat described through proprioceptive sensation (pressure, warmth, pulse) rather than emotional adjective cascading. Aftermath processed through structural metaphor ('A redistribution. Weight she had been bearing alone for six years had found a second point of support'). Closing passage is twilight-decayed: 'the stars above the Pallor's silver membrane were filtered and distant — never quite real, never fully visible.'\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"T6_stakesEscalation\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-34\\\", \\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"SCN-34\\\": \\\"Personal stakes: Kaelith's identity is on the line — will Lirien accept who she truly is? External stakes maintained: two hunter teams, observation posts, pursuit context.\\\",\\n        \\\"SCN-35\\\": \\\"Personal → relational escalation: by confessing the unsanitized Calwrath truth, Kaelith stakes the relationship on the worst thing about herself. Admission 'I would make the same call' raises stakes further — this is not asking for forgiveness but asking if Lirien can accept someone capable of this arithmetic.\\\",\\n        \\\"SCN-36\\\": \\\"Relational → irreversible: the kiss crosses a threshold that cannot be uncrossed ('I cannot undo that' / 'I do not want to undo it'). This irreversibility amplifies the stakes for ch16's betrayal reveal — chosen intimacy reframed as potential manipulation will be exponentially more devastating BECAUSE it was freely chosen here.\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Chapter 13 sits at the relational-stakes apex before the ch16 black moment. Stakes are personal (Calwrath confession), relational (first kiss), and have been structurally designed to maximize the fall when the kill contract is revealed. Correct positioning in the escalation arc.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"T7_blackMoment\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"building_toward_BM\\\": \\\"Ch13 maximizes the future devastation of the ch16 black moment through three mechanisms: (1) Kaelith explicitly frames the kiss as chosen rather than necessary ('This is not survival. This is not the bond. This is not necessity'), making the ch16 reveal that it might have been manipulation devastating precisely because of this framing; (2) Lirien's operation 31 confession creates a parallel moral weight that will be weaponized when Kaelith realizes Lirien's 43 completions include a contract on HER; (3) FS-020 plants the 'irreversible threshold' motif that ch16 will shatter.\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"No Black Moment occurs in ch13 — correctly, this is the pre-BM vulnerability peak. The chapter earns the intimacy that the BM will destroy.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"T8_internalExternalResistance\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-34\\\", \\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"SCN-34_Kaelith_internal\\\": \\\"Guilt over Calwrath (six years of self-punishment), distrust of vulnerability ('built a low wall of branches... the focused precision of a person who needed her hands occupied'), reflexive concealment ('She did not think the word. She did not need to. The body remembered before the mind permitted'). Resistance overcome by the bond making concealment impossible.\\\",\\n        \\\"SCN-35_Kaelith_internal\\\": \\\"Self-punishment-as-identity: telling Calwrath 'like a briefing. Because that was how she survived things.' Voice register as armor. The deepest resistance point: admitting 'I would make the same call. And I hate that about myself' — the resistance is to being someone who doesn't just forgive the terrible thing but would repeat it.\\\",\\n        \\\"SCN-36_Kaelith_internal\\\": \\\"Fear of judgment overcome when Lirien doesn't flinch. But new resistance surfaces: can she accept being accepted? 'Kaelith's breathing was wrong. She noticed — the shallow, too-fast rhythm the body adopted when the threat was internal, when the thing she needed protection from was her own relief.'\\\",\\n        \\\"Lirien_internal\\\": \\\"Operative conditioning against showing vulnerability. Overcome partially: shares op 31, allows hand on jaw to be 'almost a question,' uses contractions and informal language ('I don't flinch' vs her usual clinical register).\\\",\\n        \\\"external_resistance\\\": \\\"Two hunter teams, observation posts on northeastern approach, Thalen Reyvas directing pursuit from Seventh Seat. Intimacy occurs despite ongoing threat, not because threat is absent. 'The pursuit was still active' catalogued at chapter close.\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"T10_sandersonsLaws\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-34\\\", \\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"resonance_bond\\\": \\\"Bond transmits emotional states, not factual information — rule established in ch11, consistently maintained throughout ch13. 'It transmitted the agitation she was managing and the grief underneath the agitation' (emotional data). 'Not as language — it did not transmit words' (limitation stated). 'The bond carried the memory's residue — not the sound itself but the shape of it in her body' (emotional resonance, not replay). No bond-ex-machina — the bond forces honesty but does not solve any problem; Kaelith must still choose to speak.\\\",\\n        \\\"oathbrand_ghost\\\": \\\"Brand removed in ch11. Phantom ache persists: 'The place on her collarbone where the Oathbrand had lived for six years ached with the particular tenderness of a wound that no longer existed.' Consistent with removal mechanics — psychological residue, not magical persistence.\\\",\\n        \\\"returned_magic\\\": \\\"Kaelith's magic returned after Oathbrand removal. Used in closing: 'Kaelith could feel it now, with her returned senses — the Pallor's slow erosion.' Consistent with established capability restoration.\\\",\\n        \\\"quietus_pull\\\": \\\"Body-knowledge pull northeast — 'The Quietus path pulled at her bones — northeast, patient, certain.' Consistent with kinetic memory established earlier. No new magic powers introduced.\\\",\\n        \\\"fae_detection_threads\\\": \\\"Lirien places 'fae silk... enchanted to vibrate if severed.' Established fae capability, not new.\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"No magic is used to resolve conflict in this chapter — magic (the bond) creates vulnerability that the characters must navigate through speech and choice. Sanderson's First Law satisfied: all magic used is well-understood by the reader.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"T12_dualArcInterleave\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-34\\\", \\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"SCN-34\\\": \\\"Fantasy provides context (camp under pursuit threat) while romance drives the scene (bond exposing Kaelith's agitation). The bond is a magical element functioning as the romance mechanism — the arcs are structurally fused, not alternating.\\\",\\n        \\\"SCN-35\\\": \\\"Romance-dominant (Calwrath confession) but the resonance bond — a magical artifact — is the mechanism that makes concealment impossible: 'the bond would carry the lie the way it carried everything else.' Fantasy arc quiescent in this scene by design.\\\",\\n        \\\"SCN-36\\\": \\\"Romance culminates in the kiss. Chapter close re-engages fantasy arc: pursuit catalogued ('Two hunter teams remained'), Pallor erosion sensed through returned magic ('a ceiling losing structural integrity'), Quietus body-knowledge pulling northeast. Forward momentum for both arcs.\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"observations\\\": \\\"This is a romance-dominant chapter by design (first kiss, Calwrath confession). The fantasy arc is maintained as threat context and close-of-chapter forward momentum rather than actively advancing. The T12 minimum requirement ('at minimum how one arc's movement creates pressure on the other') IS met: the romance deepening (kiss) increases vulnerability that amplifies fantasy-arc stakes (if either is lost during pursuit/Quietus approach, the emotional cost is now higher). The bond-as-magic-mechanism fuses the arcs at the structural level. SCN-35 is the weakest interleave point — confession is purely romance content with only the bond providing fantasy texture.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"T13_tensionMapping\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-34\\\", \\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"SCN-34_microTension\\\": \\\"Multiple active sources: (1) pursuit — 'One approach from the southwest — visible for forty yards' catalogs threat; (2) bond exposure — Lirien's attention shifts to Kaelith's distress; (3) Calwrath memory — body remembering before mind permits; (4) will Kaelith tell the truth or maintain the lie?\\\",\\n        \\\"SCN-35_microTension\\\": \\\"Confession carries sustained tension through: (1) the content itself — war crime details escalate; (2) Kaelith's body resistance — hands shaking, throat tight, eyes closed involuntarily; (3) will Lirien stay or leave? — 'She calculated the load she could bear if Lirien left'; (4) 'I would make the same call' — the final reveal that she's not repentant, she's terrified of her own consistency.\\\",\\n        \\\"SCN-36_microTension\\\": \\\"Twelve-second counted silence after confession. Then: (5) what kind of response will Lirien give? (6) approach — who moves first? (7) 'This is not survival' — naming the choice makes it irrevocable; (8) kiss as mutual surrender; (9) aftermath — can they function with this between them? (10) pursuit still active, Pallor still failing.\\\",\\n        \\\"dead_spot_check\\\": \\\"No passage of 250+ words without at least one active tension source. The longest stretch of lower-intensity prose is the aftermath (lines 246-265), which maintains micro-tension through: hands no longer shaking (physical evidence of change), pursuit inventory, Pallor erosion, the unanswered question of 'what now.' Confirmed: zero dead spots.\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Tension level 7 (per outline: 'emotional intensity without combat'). The tension is entirely interpersonal and internal — no external action — but never flags. The 'twelve seconds of silence' (line 152) is the lowest-tension moment and is itself tense because Kaelith is counting, calculating whether Lirien will leave.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"T15_foreshadowingPayoffLedger\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-34\\\", \\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"payoffs_delivered\\\": {\\n          \\\"FS-007\\\": \\\"Calwrath battlefield decision — RESOLVED. Full unsanitized truth shared: 8-minute decision, 300 civilians, children in market, magical accelerant, temple collapse, 'I would make the same call.' This is the first time the reader receives complete details. Payoff verified present in prose.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"advanced\\\": {\\n          \\\"FS-015\\\": \\\"Resonance bond — ADVANCED. Bond used throughout for emotional transparency during confession ('the bond would carry the lie the way it carried everything else'), kiss (recursive feedback loop — 'feeling each other feel this, sensation doubled and returned and doubled again'), and aftermath ('the bond hummed between them carrying everything'). Foreshadows ch16 role (transmitting Lirien's guilt during contract revelation).\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"new_plants\\\": {\\n          \\\"FS-019\\\": \\\"Lirien's operation 31 and the name Elisi — planted. 'Number thirty-one was a merchant in Vael'thrin... He had a daughter. Seven years old. Elisi.' Parallel moral wound to Calwrath. May resurface when Lirien's Court loyalty is tested.\\\",\\n          \\\"FS-020\\\": \\\"Kiss as irreversible threshold — planted. 'I cannot undo that' / 'I do not want to undo it.' Explicitly designed to be shattered by ch16's betrayal reveal, reframing free choice as potential manipulation.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"mystery_box_closures\\\": {\\n          \\\"MB-006\\\": \\\"What really happened at the Siege of Calwrath? — CLOSED. Full answer delivered: 8-minute decision, 300 civilians including 47 children under 12, magical accelerant fire, temple collapse, Kaelith would make the same call.\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"All ledger-assigned foreshadowing activity for ch13 verified present in prose. No unlogged payoffs detected. No orphan plants.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"T16_symbolicMotifWeaving\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-34\\\", \\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"MOT-001_pallor\\\": {\\n          \\\"scene\\\": \\\"SCN-36 (closing passage)\\\",\\n          \\\"imagery\\\": \\\"'Stars above the Pallor's silver membrane were filtered and distant — never quite real, never fully visible, dimmed by the flayed skin of a god who had given themselves to fix the world in place. The membrane was thinning... a ceiling losing structural integrity. Someone was killing the sky.'\\\",\\n          \\\"evolution\\\": \\\"Act II form: failing membrane. 'Ceiling losing structural integrity' keeps the motif in Kaelith's structural-metaphor domain. Evolves from Act I 'protective barrier' to Act II 'active erosion' — appropriate progression.\\\",\\n          \\\"density\\\": \\\"1 appearance this chapter. Within 3-4 per act target.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"MOT-002_oathbrand_ghost\\\": {\\n          \\\"scene\\\": \\\"SCN-34, SCN-36\\\",\\n          \\\"imagery\\\": \\\"SCN-34: 'The place on her collarbone where the Oathbrand had lived for six years ached with the particular tenderness of a wound that no longer existed but whose absence the body had not yet registered. Phantom heat. The ghost of a verdict.' SCN-36: 'Lirien's fingers shifted. Found the hollow of Kaelith's throat where the pulse lived — not the collarbone, not the place where the Oathbrand's ghost still ached. Lower. The place where a heartbeat transmitted through skin.'\\\",\\n          \\\"evolution\\\": \\\"Post-removal form: phantom guilt. Lirien's choice to touch the pulse (life) rather than the collarbone (punishment) is a powerful visual argument — she responds to the person, not the verdict.\\\",\\n          \\\"density\\\": \\\"2 appearances. Appropriate for ghost-presence after ch11 removal.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"MOT-003_water_infiltration\\\": {\\n          \\\"scene\\\": \\\"SCN-34, SCN-36\\\",\\n          \\\"imagery\\\": \\\"SCN-34: 'Lirien's attention when she was deciding whether to press. It had a shape — narrow, focused, like water finding the place in a wall where the mortar had thinned.' SCN-36: 'I was three streets away with my hands in a fountain, and the water was very cold.'\\\",\\n          \\\"evolution\\\": \\\"Dual function: (1) Lirien-as-water infiltrating Kaelith's defenses through the wall-and-mortar structural lens (Kaelith's domain); (2) water as failed absolution in Lirien's confession — cold fountain that does not cleanse. The motif is evolving from surveillance metaphor to intimacy/guilt metaphor.\\\",\\n          \\\"density\\\": \\\"2 appearances. Within 4-5 across story target.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"MOT-004_quietus_body_knowledge\\\": {\\n          \\\"scene\\\": \\\"SCN-36 (closing passage)\\\",\\n          \\\"imagery\\\": \\\"'The Quietus path pulled at her bones — northeast, patient, certain... The path did not care what she felt or wanted or feared. The path only knew where it went.'\\\",\\n          \\\"evolution\\\": \\\"Establishing body-as-imperative: the path persists independent of emotional state. Contrasts with the emotional upheaval of the chapter — identity is in flux but destination is fixed.\\\",\\n          \\\"density\\\": \\\"1 appearance. Appropriate for Act II buildup.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"MOT-005_ythara\\\": {\\n          \\\"absent\\\": true,\\n          \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Not present in this chapter. Acceptable — MOT-005 targets 1-2 per act and is more Act III-concentrated. The Pallor erosion reference implicitly connects to Ythara's influence without naming the god directly.\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"All four expected motifs present with appropriate density and evolution. Imagery is evolving, not static — each motif appears in a new facet compared to prior chapters. MOT-005 absence justified.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"T17_voiceFingerprinting\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-34\\\", \\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"deferred_to\\\": \\\"pov-voice-maintainer (score 9/10, 2 corrections applied)\\\",\\n        \\\"independent_verification\\\": {\\n          \\\"short_declarative_sentences\\\": \\\"'Here,' she said. | 'Twelve paces deep. Eight wide. Defensible.' | 'She drove another branch into the ground. Harder.' | 'I ordered the burn.' — Confirmed 70%+ short declaratives.\\\",\\n          \\\"structural_metaphors\\\": \\\"'buttress bracing against its own weight' | 'load-bearing' | 'foundation' | 'mortar had thinned' | 'keystone carries the arch' | 'ceiling losing structural integrity' — Dominates Kaelith's metaphor space consistently.\\\",\\n          \\\"emotions_as_physical_events\\\": \\\"'heat climbing her neck, pressure behind her sternum' | 'her jaw ached' | 'fine tremor' | 'throat contracted' | 'knuckles ached' | 'hands were no longer shaking' — Zero directly named emotions in narration.\\\",\\n          \\\"military_vocabulary\\\": \\\"'assessed the position in six seconds' | 'sight line' | 'perimeter' | 'defensive' | 'operational briefings' | 'breach force' | 'embankments' | 'fire curtain' — Kaelith's entire worldview is military-architectural.\\\",\\n          \\\"formal_register\\\": \\\"'I cannot undo that.' | 'I do not want to undo it.' — No contractions in Kaelith's dialogue during emotional intensity. Formality = armor.\\\",\\n          \\\"recognition_test\\\": \\\"Opening paragraph ('Exits: two, if you counted the drop. Natural sight line... The overhang's load-bearing looked sound') is unmistakably Kaelith within 3 sentences.\\\"\\n        }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"T18_informationAsymmetry\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-34\\\", \\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"kaelith_knowledge_boundary\\\": \\\"Kaelith does not reference, think about, or act on the kill contract — correctly, she does not know it exists. Her trust in Lirien is genuine. No information-state violations.\\\",\\n        \\\"lirien_knowledge_boundary\\\": \\\"Lirien does not reveal or hint at the kill contract in any dialogue or action perceivable through Kaelith's POV. Her emotional state through the bond is read by Kaelith as genuine (which it IS — the paradox is that Lirien's feelings are real AND she holds a kill contract).\\\",\\n        \\\"bond_limitation_respected\\\": \\\"Bond transmits emotional states, not factual knowledge. Kaelith reads Lirien's emotional quality ('concern,' 'steady,' 'crack widened') but never accesses factual information about the contract. Limitation maintained consistently.\\\",\\n        \\\"reader_dramatic_irony\\\": \\\"Reader knows about the kill contract (from Lirien's POV chapters). Watching Kaelith trust Lirien with her deepest secret while the reader knows Lirien was sent to kill her creates devastating dramatic irony that amplifies every tender moment.\\\",\\n        \\\"new_information_exchanged\\\": {\\n          \\\"kaelith_to_lirien\\\": \\\"Full Calwrath truth (previously only public version known)\\\",\\n          \\\"lirien_to_kaelith\\\": \\\"Operation 31, Elisi, 43 completions (previously unknown to Kaelith and reader)\\\",\\n          \\\"to_reader\\\": \\\"Complete Calwrath details for the first time\\\"\\n        }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"T20_emotionalThroughline\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-34\\\", \\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"planned_arc\\\": \\\"defensive fear → courageous vulnerability (intensity 8)\\\",\\n        \\\"actual_arc_in_prose\\\": {\\n          \\\"opening\\\": \\\"Defensive fear — 'heat climbing her neck, pressure behind her sternum, the hyperawareness of every exit' | 'hands shaking' | displacement activity (building windbreak to avoid feeling)\\\",\\n          \\\"SCN-34_end\\\": \\\"Terrified resolve — 'She made the decision the way she made all decisions. Assess the risk. Calculate the cost. Choose.'\\\",\\n          \\\"SCN-35_mid\\\": \\\"Raw exposure — 'Her voice had dropped. She did not raise it.' | 'Her hands pressed the stone so hard her knuckles ached.' | eyes closing involuntarily\\\",\\n          \\\"SCN-35_end\\\": \\\"Annihilating vulnerability — counting silence ('Twelve seconds. Fifteen. Twenty.'), calculating load-bearing capacity for Lirien's departure\\\",\\n          \\\"SCN-36_pivot\\\": \\\"Overwhelmed relief — 'Kaelith's throat closed. Not metaphorically.' | breathing wrong ('shallow, too-fast rhythm... the thing she needed protection from was her own relief')\\\",\\n          \\\"SCN-36_end\\\": \\\"Terrified hope — 'Her hands were no longer shaking' | 'Something had changed in the architecture. Not a collapse. A redistribution.' | 'The terror of it was indistinguishable from the hope'\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"matches_throughline_chart\\\": \\\"Yes — transitions from 'exposed fear' (dominantEmotionStart) to 'courageous vulnerability' (dominantEmotionEnd) with intensity 8. Pivot at Lirien's 'I don't flinch' matches planned pivot. CHAR-002's emotional state (fierce tenderness) readable through Kaelith's bond perception.\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"T21_vulnerabilityLadder\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"ladder_step\\\": \\\"Step 4 — sharing the unforgivable parts\\\",\\n        \\\"kaelith_vulnerability\\\": \\\"Shares complete Calwrath truth including: 8-minute decision, 300 civilians, children, accelerant fire, temple collapse. Culminates in 'I would make the same call. And I hate that about myself.' This is not just a confession — it's admitting she is the person who would do this again. Step 4 requires sharing the thing you believe makes you monstrous.\\\",\\n        \\\"lirien_reciprocity\\\": \\\"Shares operation 31 — merchant in Vael'thrin, daughter Elisi (age 7), clean arithmetic concealing moral devastation. Retains the daughter's name against Seep training ('I was not supposed to remember it'). Equivalent moral weight to Calwrath — different scale, same kind of wound.\\\",\\n        \\\"kiss_as_response\\\": \\\"Kiss emerges from mutual vulnerability, not as reward. Framed as recognition ('the specific, deliberate pressure of two people who had held themselves apart for weeks and had finally, consciously, chosen to stop'). NOT framed as romantic reward for bravery or redemption through love.\\\",\\n        \\\"escalation_from_prior\\\": \\\"Previous steps involved sharing information (step 1), physical proximity tolerance (step 2), admitting need (step 3). Step 4 escalates to sharing the thing you believe disqualifies you from connection. Clear upward progression.\\\",\\n        \\\"physical_parallel\\\": \\\"Physical vulnerability (kiss) escalates in parallel with emotional vulnerability (confession). Physical does not precede emotional — the kiss follows the mutual confession, confirming that emotional vulnerability earns physical intimacy.\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"T23_mysteryBoxInventory\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PARTIAL\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-35\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"closures\\\": {\\n          \\\"MB-006\\\": \\\"'What really happened at the Siege of Calwrath?' — CLOSED in this chapter. Full answer delivered through Kaelith's confession to Lirien. Reader receives complete details for the first time.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"openings\\\": \\\"No new mystery boxes opened in this chapter. FS-019 (Lirien's operation 31) and FS-020 (kiss as irreversible threshold) are foreshadowing plants, not reader questions.\\\",\\n        \\\"active_count_post_ch13\\\": 12,\\n        \\\"target_range\\\": \\\"3-7\\\",\\n        \\\"issue\\\": \\\"Active mystery box count (12) exceeds the 3-7 target range specified in T23. However, this is a plotting-level structural concern: 10 of the 12 boxes were opened in chapters 1-11 and are scheduled for resolution in chapters 16-22. The chapter-level behavior is correct — MB-006 closes on schedule, no inappropriate boxes are opened. The excess reflects the story's conspiracy-thriller complexity (dual conspiracies, multiple information layers) rather than a drafting failure.\\\",\\n        \\\"foregrounded_questions\\\": \\\"At this story point, the reader is actively tracking approximately 5-6 questions: (1) Will the kill contract be discovered? (2) Can Lirien find a loophole? (3) Who is poisoning the Pallor? (4) What is the Quietus? (5) Will trust survive betrayal? (6) What is the Seep's true agenda? The remaining boxes (MB-001 partially answered, MB-010 background) are ambient backstory.\\\",\\n        \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Flag for plotting-level review but do not penalize this chapter's draft. The chapter correctly manages its assigned box closures and does not contribute to the excess.\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"T24_subtextInDialogue\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-34\\\", \\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"SCN-34_subtext\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"line\\\": \\\"'You're building a windbreak that will not break wind.'\\\",\\n            \\\"surface\\\": \\\"Practical observation about camp construction\\\",\\n            \\\"subtext\\\": \\\"'I see you avoiding something through displacement activity, and I'm choosing to name it gently rather than pressing directly.'\\\",\\n            \\\"gap_quality\\\": \\\"Wide gap — the observation is factual but the intent is emotional. Effective.\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"line\\\": \\\"'What are you afraid of?'\\\",\\n            \\\"surface\\\": \\\"Direct question about Kaelith's emotional state\\\",\\n            \\\"subtext\\\": \\\"'The bond means neither of us can hide. I'm asking you to choose trust deliberately, knowing the bond will reveal any evasion.'\\\",\\n            \\\"gap_quality\\\": \\\"Medium gap — question is direct but the implied stakes (bond makes lying futile) are unstated.\\\"\\n          }\\n        ],\\n        \\\"SCN-35_subtext\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"line\\\": \\\"Entire confession delivered as operational briefing\\\",\\n            \\\"surface\\\": \\\"Tactical debrief — objective, constraints, decision matrix, outcome\\\",\\n            \\\"subtext\\\": \\\"'This is who I am. I am capable of terrible necessary things. This is the worst thing about me and I need you to see it.'\\\",\\n            \\\"gap_quality\\\": \\\"Wide gap — the format (briefing) actively conceals the emotional content (self-exposure). The restraint IS the subtext.\\\"\\n          }\\n        ],\\n        \\\"SCN-36_subtext\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"line\\\": \\\"'You are not asking for forgiveness. You're asking if I flinch.'\\\",\\n            \\\"surface\\\": \\\"Analysis of what Kaelith is actually doing\\\",\\n            \\\"subtext\\\": \\\"'I see through your armor to the actual need underneath it, and I'm telling you I'm capable of meeting that need.'\\\",\\n            \\\"gap_quality\\\": \\\"Narrow but devastating — Lirien names the subtext, which is itself a form of intimacy (being truly seen).\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"line\\\": \\\"'I don't flinch.'\\\",\\n            \\\"surface\\\": \\\"Statement of character/capability\\\",\\n            \\\"subtext\\\": \\\"'I see everything you just showed me and I'm staying. Not because I absolve you — because I refuse to look away.'\\\",\\n            \\\"gap_quality\\\": \\\"Wide gap — three words carrying the weight of acceptance-without-absolution.\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"line\\\": \\\"'This is not survival. This is not the bond. This is not necessity.'\\\",\\n            \\\"surface\\\": \\\"Negation — naming what this moment is NOT\\\",\\n            \\\"subtext\\\": \\\"'I am choosing you freely. The bond did not make me want this. Survival did not make me need this. I want this because I want YOU.'\\\",\\n            \\\"gap_quality\\\": \\\"Medium gap — the negations circle around the unsaid positive (desire/choice). TP-3 thematic argument delivered through absence.\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"line\\\": \\\"'I can feel you.'\\\",\\n            \\\"surface\\\": \\\"Bond mechanics — she can sense Kaelith's emotional state\\\",\\n            \\\"subtext\\\": \\\"'I feel everything about you — all of it, the fear and the wanting and the relief — and I'm choosing to stay inside that feeling.'\\\",\\n            \\\"gap_quality\\\": \\\"Wide gap — four words that could be clinical (bond report) but are intimate (radical acceptance).\\\"\\n          }\\n        ],\\n        \\\"no_on_the_nose\\\": \\\"No dialogue line states its subtext directly. Even Lirien's 'You're asking if I flinch' — which names Kaelith's hidden need — delivers this through analytical framing rather than emotional declaration. Characters never say 'I accept you' or 'I love you' or 'I forgive you.'\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"T25_thematicArgumentScaffolding\\\": {\\n      \\\"grade\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n      \\\"scenes\\\": [\\\"SCN-34\\\", \\\"SCN-35\\\", \\\"SCN-36\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n        \\\"TP1_trust_as_structural_failure\\\": {\\n          \\\"dramatization\\\": \\\"Kaelith deliberately exposes her worst self to someone who could weaponize it. The bond makes concealment impossible, but the CHOICE to speak is Kaelith's. Trust-through-deliberate-risk: 'She made the decision the way she made all decisions. Assess the risk. Calculate the cost. Choose.' Trust requires vulnerability to someone who can destroy you — and Lirien could destroy Kaelith with this knowledge.\\\",\\n          \\\"embodied_not_stated\\\": true,\\n          \\\"Act2_testing\\\": \\\"The 'easy answer' (maintaining the sanitized Calwrath version) is explicitly rejected. The harder truth is chosen.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"TP2_price_of_the_right_choice\\\": {\\n          \\\"dramatization\\\": \\\"Calwrath IS this pillar dramatized: 'Eight hundred soldiers. Three hundred civilians. The time constraint. The available options.' The right tactical choice cost 300 lives including 47 children. There is no clean resolution — 'I would make the same call. And I hate that about myself.' The price is not just the deaths but living as the person who would choose those deaths again.\\\",\\n          \\\"embodied_not_stated\\\": true,\\n          \\\"irreconcilable_dilemma\\\": true\\n        },\\n        \\\"TP3_chosen_vs_only\\\": {\\n          \\\"dramatization\\\": \\\"'This is not survival. This is not the bond. This is not necessity.' The kiss is explicitly framed as the first freely chosen intimacy. TP-3 argues that love born from necessity demands a 'second act' of free choice — this is that second act. The chapter dramatizes the cage opening: they COULD maintain professional distance, they COULD attribute attraction to the bond, they CHOOSE not to.\\\",\\n          \\\"embodied_not_stated\\\": true,\\n          \\\"explicitly_tested\\\": \\\"The negations ('not survival, not the bond, not necessity') are the test — Kaelith must reject every comfortable explanation before the choice is real.\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"All three thematic pillars are advanced through character action and dialogue. No pillar is stated through narration or internal monologue summary. Theme is embodied by characters, not explained to the reader.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"secondPassFindings\\\": {\\n    \\\"MRU_ordering\\\": {\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"clean\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Although T14 (MRU) is excluded from the craft profile, paragraph-level stimulus-response ordering was checked. Key sequence at the kiss approach: involuntary pull closer ('Kaelith did not remember deciding to move') → conscious awareness (bond registering convergence) → deliberate declaration ('This is not survival') → voluntary action ('She closed the distance'). The involuntary-to-voluntary gradient is well-structured. Confession sequence: body remembers before mind permits (involuntary) → displacement activity as coping (semi-voluntary) → choice to speak (voluntary). No MRU ordering violations found.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"microTension_dead_spots\\\": {\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"clean\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Full scan completed. No passage of 250+ words without at least one active tension source. Lowest-intensity passage is the aftermath (lines 246-265), which maintains tension through: physical evidence of change (steady hands), pursuit inventory, Pallor erosion, and the fundamental uncertainty of 'what now.' The twelve-second counted silence (line 152-154) is the lowest-intensity MOMENT but is itself tense through Kaelith counting and calculating collapse scenarios.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"show_dont_tell\\\": {\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"clean\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Although SDT is not a standalone craft tool, it's enforced through the style guide. Scan found emotions consistently shown through physical tells: jaw ache, heat climbing neck, pressure behind sternum, hand tremor, throat closure, breathing rhythm changes. Two instances of named emotions: 'concern' (line 90, perceived through bond — acceptable as bond data) and 'the terror of it was indistinguishable from the hope' (line 272 — juxtaposed and treated as indistinguishable, which is itself a form of showing). Show:tell ratio estimated at 92:8, consistent with metadata claim.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"sceneBySceneAudit\\\": {\\n    \\\"SCN-34\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"sequel (per outline)\\\",\\n      \\\"value_shift\\\": \\\"concealment → exposure\\\",\\n      \\\"tools_checked\\\": 16,\\n      \\\"tools_passed\\\": 16,\\n      \\\"key_observation\\\": \\\"Sequel structure executed through Kaelith's processing of ch12 events: the bond forces emotional transparency that makes concealment impossible. The dilemma (tell the truth or maintain the sanitized version) is resolved through conscious choice, not external pressure. The windbreak-building displacement activity is an excellent show-don't-tell mechanism for avoidance.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"SCN-35\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"scene (per outline)\\\",\\n      \\\"value_shift\\\": \\\"control → surrender\\\",\\n      \\\"tools_checked\\\": 16,\\n      \\\"tools_passed\\\": 16,\\n      \\\"key_observation\\\": \\\"The confession scene is the craft centerpiece of the chapter. Delivered as tactical briefing (voice fingerprinting), hiding emotional devastation under procedural language (subtext), with the body betraying the cost (show-don't-tell). The final admission ('I would make the same call') is the scene's disaster — worse than the deaths themselves because it means Kaelith's identity includes this capability. TP-2 dramatized at its sharpest.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"SCN-36\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"scene (per outline)\\\",\\n      \\\"value_shift\\\": \\\"anticipated rejection → irreversible intimacy\\\",\\n      \\\"tools_checked\\\": 16,\\n      \\\"tools_passed\\\": 15,\\n      \\\"tools_partial\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"partial_tool\\\": \\\"T23 (aggregate count concern, not scene-level)\\\",\\n      \\\"key_observation\\\": \\\"The kiss scene demonstrates exceptional craft discipline: the approach is built through proprioceptive detail (distance measured, breathing changes, bond amplification), the kiss itself avoids both purple prose and clinical detachment, and the aftermath processes through structural metaphor ('A redistribution. Weight she had been bearing alone for six years had found a second point of support'). Lirien's hand finding the throat-hollow (pulse) rather than the collarbone (Oathbrand ghost) is a symbolic masterclass — she chooses life over verdict.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"artifactsRead\\\": [\\n    \\\"craft-profile.json\\\",\\n    \\\"chapters/013/draft.md\\\",\\n    \\\"chapters/013/metadata.json\\\",\\n    \\\"plot/chapter-outlines/chapter-013.json\\\",\\n    \\\"craft-tracking/symbolic-motif-registry.json\\\",\\n    \\\"craft-tracking/mystery-box-inventory.json\\\",\\n    \\\"continuity/foreshadowing-