d 'Lirien had spent thirteen chapters learning to recognize and six chapters failing to classify' — meta-reference breaking fourth wall. Changed to 'weeks learning to recognize and days failing to classify' to use in-world time.\\\",\\n        \\\"before\\\": \\\"the specific warmth that Lirien had spent thirteen chapters learning to recognize and six chapters failing to classify\\\",\\n        \\\"after\\\": \\\"the specific warmth that Lirien had spent weeks learning to recognize and days failing to classify\\\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"noChangeNeeded\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"Vocabulary Level\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Operational vocabulary deployed consistently: 'operational' (10x), 'contract' (17x), 'tactical' (6x), 'classify' (5x), 'assessment' (5x), 'parameter' (3x), 'protocol' (2x), 'perimeter' (3x), 'catalogued' (2x). Intelligence-operative register maintained throughout.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"Sentence Rhythm\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Mean 12.9 words, median 9 words. Distribution: very short 35.3%, short 20.9%, medium 18.6%, long 11.6%, very long 13.6%. Matches Lirien's 'mixed and fluid' fingerprint with cataloguing fragments and longer analytical passages. Combat scene shows appropriate shortening to field-note bursts. Emotional destabilization moments ('Get up. She's still fighting. Move.' / 'This woman. This warmth.') correctly drop to 3-8 word fragments.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"Metaphor Domain\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Water/infiltration dominant: 'water' (13x), 'surface' (7x), 'current' (4x), 'seep' (3x), 'harbour' (3x), 'dissolve' (2x), 'tidewater,' 'undertow,' 'ripple,' 'flood,' 'depth' — extensive and correct. Architectural metaphors present (12 instances) but ALL are appropriate: 8 describe Kaelith or her qualities (intimacy bleed-through), 3 are self-applied in post-intimacy context (shows Kaelith's language infiltrating Lirien's self-perception — thematically correct for ch14), 1 is the deliberate thematic merger ('Contracts were architecture'). No stray architectural metaphors unconnected to Kaelith influence.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"Emotional Register\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Zero instances of direct emotional labeling ('she felt sad/angry/afraid'). Classification-first pattern maintained: 'Risk assessment: catastrophic' before kissing, 'Breathe. Classify. Contain.' during guilt, 'Mission parameters, redefined' for resolution. Classification correctly fails during intimacy ('she couldn't classify it') and during guilt ('She could not classify this'). Breakthrough moments are simple: 'She kissed Kaelith anyway' and 'it had felt right.' Simplification = surrender.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"Attention Priority\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"All three scene openings are people-first. Scene 1: 'Three people in the treeline.' Scene 2: 'Lirien found Kaelith' then explicit 'People first.' annotation with detailed face-reading. Scene 3: Opens with Kaelith's dialogue and voice quality. Architecture described only after people in every case.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"Contraction Usage\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Contractions present and natural for ch14 arc position: didn't (8x), don't (6x), I'm (4x), she'd (4x), couldn't (2x), doesn't (2x), wasn't (2x), hadn't (2x), It's (3x), there's (3x), You're (3x), That's (2x), They'd (2x), I've (2x), and single instances of can't, haven't, shouldn't, wouldn't, She's. Present in both internal monologue and speech. Not universal — formal phrasing still present ('She could not classify this,' 'I do not want to undo it' in ch13 carryover). Appropriate evolution.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"Combat Voice (Scene 1)\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Peak operational vocabulary: 'registered the configuration,' 'military-grade shaping,' 'Classic isolation protocol,' 'separation geometry,' 'triangulated dead zone.' Cataloguing fragments as field notes: 'Three people in the treeline. Two behind granite, one elevated.' / 'Designed for her. Specifically.' Bond perception described through non-architectural metaphors: 'compass needle finding north,' 'lamp carried through a dark house,' 'surfacing from deep water.' Combat rhythm is fast but analytical — Lirien observes and assesses even under fire, distinct from Kaelith's instinctive action-first combat.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"Intimate Scene Voice (Scene 2)\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Classification system under visible strain: operational language provides scaffold ('Risk assessment: catastrophic') but fails to contain the experience ('the precision crumbled almost immediately'). Water metaphors deployed for boundary dissolution ('like sugar in warm water,' 'like water through packed earth'). The Seep metaphor made explicit and thematically resonant. Emotional breakthroughs arrive as simplifications: 'She kissed Kaelith anyway,' 'The specificity destroyed her,' 'This could not be contained.'\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"Guilt Section Voice (Scene 3)\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Classification system weaponized against self: 'The guilt was structural, not situational.' Contract analysis becomes loophole discovery — the operative mind turned toward salvation rather than execution. Tidewater metaphor for guilt ('Seeping. Rising through the cracks') is perfectly in-domain. The internal monologue italicized passage ('I will solve this. I will find the exact margin. I will kill you for three seconds...') shows first-person declarations flooding through — the 'I will' repetition signals determination breaking through classification. Mission parameters redefined in operational language: 'Not execute target. Save target from contract.'\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"Paragraph Opening Variety\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"She + The combined: 21.3% (35 of 164 paragraphs). Well under the 30% threshold flagged in ch13 audit. Good variety in openers: Lirien/Lirien's (17), Through (7), dialogue (12+), Not (6), Kaelith/Kaelith's (10), A (5), But (5).\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"Sensory Signature\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Visual/auditory primary in observation scenes (36 visual terms, 17 auditory). Tactile count (56) elevated but expected given Scene 2's physical intimacy — bond transmission of physical sensation inherently involves tactile perception. In non-intimate passages, visual dominates (face-reading, tracking movement, light/dawn descriptions). Auditory present in suppression field perception ('crackled,' 'humming'), voice quality assessment, and silence descriptions.\\\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"observationsForDownstreamAgents\\\": [\\n      \\\"The word 'structural' appears 6-7 times as an architectural modifier — always thematically motivated but the repetition may be noticeable. Line editor may wish to vary vocabulary (e.g., 'foundational,' 'load-bearing') in 1-2 instances while preserving the thematic throughline.\\\",\\n      \\\"Line 170 has a complex grammatical structure ('Kaelith Maren, who had held walls... letting a sound like that escape was its own kind of structural event') where the participial phrase's subject is ambiguous. Line editor may wish to tighten.\\\",\\n      \\\"Kaelith architectural metaphor bleed-through is extensive (12 instances) and all thematically justified, but the concentration in Scene 3 (6 instances in 8 paragraphs, lines 260-326) is dense. This is likely intentional — Lirien's post-intimacy state shows maximum infiltration — but the craft enforcer should verify this density serves the scene.\\\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \\\"artifactsRead\\\": [\\n    \\\"chapters/014/draft.md\\\",\\n    \\\"characters/CHAR-002.json (voiceFingerprint section)\\\",\\n    \\\"style/style-guide.json (perPOVCalibration for CHAR-002)\\\",\\n    \\\"chapters/014/metadata.json\\\",\\n    \\\"chapters/013/draft.md (final 50 lines — POV transition check)\\\",\\n    \\\"chapters/012/draft.md (opening — voice comparison)\\\",\\n    \\\"chapters/010/draft.md (opening — voice comparison)\\\",\\n    \\\"chapters/008/draft.md (opening — voice comparison)\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"artifactsWritten\\\": [\\n    \\\"chapters/014/draft.md (1 correction applied)\\\",\\n    \\\"agents/pov-voice-maintainer/status.json\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\nSTATUSEOF\\necho \\\"Status written successfully\\\"\", \"description\": \"Write agent status file\", \"initial_wait\": 10}"
