vastating. Verify the emotional investment is being constructed.\\n4. **T8 — Internal and External Resistance**: Both characters' resistance layers present. Lirien: operative conditioning vs attachment, contract vs desire. Kaelith: trust issues, self-worth.\\n5. **T10 — Sanderson's Laws**: Magic used in combat follows established rules. Bond mechanics consistent. No magic solving problems without prior establishment.\\n6. **T12 — Dual-Arc Interleave**: Fantasy arc (combat/ambush) and romance arc (intimacy) interweave — combat tests the bond which enables the intimacy. Neither arc floats free of the other.\\n7. **T13 — Tension Mapping**: Tension level appropriate for ch14 (target: 8). Combat high, post-intimacy has different tension (emotional), Scene 3 ramps tension through guilt/secret.\\n8. **T15 — Foreshadowing/Payoff**: FACT-008 (contract loophole) planted. Check for other foreshadowing plants and any payoffs of earlier plants.\\n9. **T16 — Symbolic Motif Weaving**: Four motifs should appear: Pallor (MOT-001), Oathbrand ghost (MOT-002), Water/infiltration (MOT-003), Quietus body-knowledge (MOT-004). Verify presence and appropriate imagery.\\n10. **T17 — Voice Fingerprinting**: Lirien's voice distinct from Kaelith's throughout. (POV voice maintainer scored 95/100, but verify from craft perspective.)\\n11. **T18 — Information Asymmetry**: Kaelith doesn't know about contract. Reader knows. Lirien hides it. Verify asymmetry is maintained and creates dramatic irony.\\n12. **T20 — Emotional Throughline**: Lirien's emotional arc this chapter: fierce focus → cautious surrender → guilty determination. Verify progression is clear and consistent.\\n13. **T21 — Vulnerability Ladder**: Step 5 — physical intimacy. Verify it feels earned by steps 1-4 and represents genuine escalation.\\n14. **T23 — Mystery Box Inventory**: Active mystery boxes maintained. MB-008 (contract loophole) should advance from \\\"open\\\" to \\\"partially answered.\\\"\\n15. **T24 — Subtext in Dialogue**: Every charged Kaelith-Lirien exchange should have at least one sentence where implied meaning exceeds literal meaning.\\n16. **T25 — Thematic Argument Scaffolding**: All three thematic pillars advanced: TP-1 (trust through vulnerability to destruction), TP-2 (price of the right choice — hiding contract), TP-3 (chosen vs only — intimacy is chosen).\\n\\n## Prose Quality Floor Checks\\n- Max 2 clichés per chapter\\n- Max 3 adverbs per page (approx 250 words)\\n- Show-to-tell ratio target: 90:10\\n- All banned phrases absent\\n- Every metaphor from POV character's domains\\n- Max 6 unbroken dialogue lines without beat\\n- Max 2 consecutive reflective paragraphs without action/dialogue\\n- No modern slang\\n- Paragraph opening variety (avoid 30%+ She/The)\\n\\n## Output\\n- If edits needed: Make them directly to `chapters/014/draft.md`\\n- Write your status to `agents/craft-enforcer/status.json` with result \\\"completed\\\" (if craft compliance is achieved or has been fixed) or \\\"blocked\\\" (if fundamental craft failures that cannot be fixed)\\n- Include in your status: per-tool compliance verdicts, any changes made, overall craft score\\n- Update `craft-tracking/symbolic-motif-registry.json` with ch14 motif appearances if not already updated\"}"
