ching a wall that remembered bearing weight it no longer carried.' Beneath it: Kaelith's heartbeat.\\\",\\n            \\\"function\\\": \\\"The ghost of institutional punishment persists even after removal — absence as its own form of presence. Lirien's attention to the heartbeat beneath the ghost foreshadows the loophole: the heartbeat is both proof of life and mechanism of contract fulfillment. Evolution: from physical wound (Act I) to phantom memory (Act II), the brand becoming metaphor for institutional damage that outlasts the institution.\\\"\\n        })\\n    elif motif['id'] == 'MOT-003':\\n        motif['appearances'].append({\\n            \\\"chapter\\\": 14,\\n            \\\"scene\\\": \\\"SCN-37, SCN-38, SCN-39\\\",\\n            \\\"imagery\\\": \\\"Maximum deployment chapter. Combat: 'surfacing from deep water' (suppression field collapse). Intimacy: 'like sugar in warm water' (boundary dissolution), 'water through packed earth' (warmth spreading from kiss), 'current beneath still water' (desire). Guilt: 'tidewater — not crashing, not dramatic. Seeping.' (guilt rising through cracks). Identity: Seep naming metaphor made explicit — 'She was the water, and Kaelith was the structure, and the structure was opening to her.' Post-intimacy: scene viewed 'through water.' Quietus path: 'the way water knew downhill.'\\\",\\n            \\\"function\\\": \\\"Water-as-Lirien reaches peak density in the chapter where infiltration becomes mutual. Seven distinct water images spanning combat, intimacy, guilt, and identity. Tidewater guilt is the key evolution: water as both connection and corrosion. The Seep metaphor made explicit connects Lirien's organizational identity to her personal method of love — both find every crack. Evolution: from operative precision (Act I) to intimacy-as-infiltration (Act II), now encompassing guilt, desire, and identity crisis simultaneously.\\\"\\n        })\\n    elif motif['id'] == 'MOT-004':\\n        motif['appearances'].append({\\n            \\\"chapter\\\": 14,\\n            \\\"scene\\\": \\\"SCN-39\\\",\\n            \\\"imagery\\\": \\\"'Northeast. The pull is stronger today.' Path calling through bone and kinetic memory. 'Kaelith's body knew the way the way water knew downhill — not through decision but through nature, through the deep grammar of what she was.'\\\",\\n            \\\"function\\\": \\\"Quietus pull intensifying as they approach. Notably described through Lirien's water-domain metaphor ('the way water knew downhill'), showing intimacy bleeding into perception — Lirien understands Kaelith's body-knowledge through her own metaphorical framework. The cross-domain metaphor fusion (body-knowledge + water) reflects how the two women's ways of understanding the world are converging.\\\"\\n        })\\n\\ndata['lastUpdatedChapter'] = 14\\ndata['notes'] = \\\"Updated through chapter 14. All four primary motifs tracked with ch14 appearances. MOT-003 (water/infiltration) reaches peak deployment in ch14 with 7 distinct images. MOT-005 (Ythara) has no ch14 appearance — appropriate since Ythara is background threat, not foregrounded in this intimate/combat chapter.\\\"\\n\\nwith open('craft-tracking/symbolic-motif-registry.json', 'w') as f:\\n    json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\\n\\nprint(\\\"✅ Motif registry updated for ch14\\\")\\nPYEOF\", \"description\": \"Update motif registry for ch14\", \"initial_wait\": 10}"
