              "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd /home/jakubs/repositories/books/romantasy-book-1/.romantic-fantasy-writer/stories/001 && python3 << 'PYEOF'\\nimport json\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\n\\nstatus = {\\n    \\\"agent\\\": \\\"craft-enforcer\\\",\\n    \\\"chapter\\\": 14,\\n    \\\"result\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n    \\\"timestamp\\\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\\n    \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Chapter 14 craft enforcement audit completed. Systematic scene-by-scene and tool-by-tool verification of all 16 active craft tools against 3 scenes (SCN-37, SCN-38, SCN-39). All 16 tools PASS. 4 prose corrections applied: (1) removed banned word 'suddenly' from line 84, (2) inserted physical/bond beat in loophole discovery section to break 12-paragraph reflective run, (3) inserted second physical beat (pulse point) to further break reflective stretch, (4) inserted physical beat at end of Scene 1 post-combat analysis to break 5-paragraph reflective run. Maximum consecutive reflective paragraphs reduced from 12 to 3. Symbolic motif registry updated with ch14 appearances for all 4 motifs. Overall craft compliance: 9.7/10.\\\",\\n    \\\"craftToolCompliance\\\": {\\n        \\\"T5_toneContract\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 10,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"SCN-37\\\": \\\"Combat handled without glamorization. Bond-dependency framed as 'dangerous equation' not triumph. No forbidden tones detected.\\\",\\n                \\\"SCN-38\\\": \\\"Intimacy rendered through sensation and meaning, not purple prose or sentimentality. 'Risk assessment: catastrophic. She kissed Kaelith anyway.' — unsentimental, direct. Neither character apologizes afterward.\\\",\\n                \\\"SCN-39\\\": \\\"Guilt described as 'tidewater — not crashing, not dramatic. Seeping.' Self-aware avoidance of melodrama. Loophole discovery cold-precise. Closing image twilight-toned: 'The real sky was darker than the false one. Less kind. But it was true.'\\\"\\n            },\\n            \\\"forbiddenTones\\\": \\\"None detected. No whimsy, no grimdark nihilism, no melodrama, no camp, no epic-triumphant, no pedagogical exposition.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"T6_stakesEscalation\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 10,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"survivalStakes\\\": \\\"Ambush designed with intelligence about their specific capabilities — Thalen's network has studied them. Suppression field targets Lirien specifically.\\\",\\n                \\\"emotionalStakes\\\": \\\"Physical intimacy is 'the first thing they do that cannot be defended as survival necessity.' Escalated from ch13's first kiss.\\\",\\n                \\\"betrayalStakes\\\": \\\"Kaelith says 'someone I want tomorrows with' while Lirien hides the contract. Loophole discovery raises stakes: 'stop a heart wrong, and it stayed stopped.'\\\"\\n            }\\n        },\\n        \\\"T7_blackMomentSetup\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 10,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Every intimate moment in this chapter deepens the devastation of ch16's reveal. Kaelith's generous trust ('I'm choosing not to demand the inventory'), her future-imagining ('someone I want tomorrows with'), and the physical surrender all create emotional investment that the black moment will shatter. Lirien's hidden loophole plan adds another betrayal layer — she had a solution and didn't share it.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"T8_internalExternalResistance\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 9,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"lirienInternal\\\": \\\"Operative conditioning vs. attachment: training 'clamping down on the first-person declaration.' Contract vs. desire: 'the contractual mechanism of their destruction.' Professional containment crumbling: 'Risk assessment: catastrophic. She kissed Kaelith anyway.'\\\",\\n                \\\"kaelithInternal\\\": \\\"Trust issues: 'a woman whose life had taught her that trust was the structural failure that preceded collapse.' Self-worth: 'joy were a structural material Kaelith had never worked with and wasn't certain would hold.' Military discipline yielding.\\\",\\n                \\\"external\\\": \\\"Thalen's hunters (coordinated ambush), kill contract binding, time pressure (Pallor erosion, pursuit, reinforcements incoming).\\\"\\n            }\\n        },\\n        \\\"T10_sandersonsLaws\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 10,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"magicRules\\\": \\\"Suppression field creates clear limitation (40% capacity). Every manipulation has visible cost ('drawing thread through wet sand'). Bond capability previously established in ch11-13.\\\",\\n                \\\"noDeusExMachina\\\": \\\"Victory through tactical coordination, not new powers. Suppression field forces precision over power. Loophole based on established contract wording, not new magic.\\\",\\n                \\\"bondConsistency\\\": \\\"Bond transmits sensation (pain, heartbeat, emotional quality) but not factual content — consistent with established rules. Kaelith senses weight but not specifics of contract.\\\"\\n            }\\n        },\\n        \\\"T12_dualArcInterleave\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 10,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"SCN-37\\\": \\\"Fantasy threat (ambush) tests romance bond. Combat synchronization proves mutual dependence — the relationship IS the weapon.\\\",\\n                \\\"SCN-38\\\": \\\"Post-combat adrenaline drives intimacy — survival demands acknowledgment through bodies. Bond makes intimacy recursive (fantasy mechanism enables romance depth).\\\",\\n                \\\"SCN-39\\\": \\\"Romance hope (Vael Seren) activates contract guilt (fantasy complication). Loophole plan requires the bond (romance tool becomes contract-escape mechanism). 'The bond that made them deadly in combat could save Kaelith's life by stopping it.'\\\"\\n            },\\n            \\\"arcBalance\\\": \\\"Neither arc floats free. Every romance moment has fantasy consequence; every fantasy element enables or complicates the romance.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"T13_tensionMapping\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 9,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"SCN-37_tension\\\": \\\"9-10: Active combat, life-threatening, suppression field, shared pain through bond.\\\",\\n                \\\"SCN-38_tension\\\": \\\"7-8: Charged physical proximity, first full intimacy in dangerous location (4 incapacitated attackers within 100 paces), bond feedback loop.\\\",\\n                \\\"SCN-39_tension\\\": \\\"7-8: Guilt as tidewater, contract secret during tender conversation, loophole with absolute risk, reinforcements incoming.\\\",\\n                \\\"chapterAverage\\\": 8,\\n                \\\"microTensionNote\\\": \\\"Post-correction: no passage longer than 3 paragraphs without physical grounding. Loophole section maintains intellectual tension (life-or-death consequences of the plan) even during internal analysis.\\\"\\n            }\\n        },\\n        \\\"T15_foreshadowingPayoff\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 10,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"planted\\\": [\\n                    \\\"FS-012: Contract loophole — 'cessation of heartbeat' as state not duration. Planted in Lirien's internal analysis.\\\",\\n                    \\\"Vael Seren harbour — Lirien's capacity for desire outside operational parameters.\\\",\\n                    \\\"Thalen's intelligence on Lirien's specific capabilities — suppression field designed for fae resonance.\\\"\\n                ],\\n                \\\"advanced\\\": [\\n                    \\\"FS-015: Resonance bond advanced — demonstrated as combat force multiplier and intimate feedback mechanism. Foreshadows essential role in ch20 loophole execution.\\\"\\n                ],\\n                \\\"payoffs\\\": \\\"No formal payoffs in this chapter (appropriate).\\\",\\n                \\\"noUnloggedPayoffs\\\": True\\n            }\\n        },\\n        \\\"T16_symbolicMotifWeaving\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 10,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"MOT-001_pallor\\\": \\\"3 appearances: opening (thinning membrane), Scene 3 (through water), closing (false sky vs true sky). Evolution from passive failure to active deception metaphor.\\\",\\n                \\\"MOT-002_oathbrand\\\": \\\"2 appearances: phantom itch through bond (post-combat), ghost as 'wall that remembered bearing weight' (post-intimacy). Evolution from physical wound to memory-presence.\\\",\\n                \\\"MOT-003_water\\\": \\\"7+ appearances: surfacing (suppression collapse), sugar dissolving (intimacy), tidewater (guilt), Seep naming explicit, current (desire), through water (scene quality), downhill (Quietus). PEAK DEPLOYMENT chapter. Water as connection AND corrosion.\\\",\\n                \\\"MOT-004_quietus\\\": \\\"1 appearance: 'The pull is stronger today.' Cross-domain metaphor with water ('the way water knew downhill'). Appropriate density for Lirien POV (body-knowledge is Kaelith's domain).\\\"\\n            },\\n            \\\"motifRegistryUpdated\\\": True\\n        },\\n        \\\"T17_voiceFingerprinting\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 10,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"lirienVoice\\\": \\\"Observation→interpretation structure ('Three people in the treeline. Two behind granite, one elevated.'). Intelligence-operative vocabulary (operational parameters, probability tree, extraction point, status report). Water/infiltration metaphors throughout. Cataloguing habits. Emotional destabilization through sentence shortening ('Get up. She's still fighting. Move.'). Contractions present in internal monologue per arc progression.\\\",\\n                \\\"kaelithVoice\\\": \\\"Distinct in dialogue: short, structural, direct ('That's enough,' 'I know they exist,' 'Inside'). Military/structural frame ('load-bearing specifications' implied). Patience as structural integrity.\\\",\\n                \\\"distinction\\\": \\\"A reader could identify Lirien's POV within the first paragraph without being told.\\\"\\n            }\\n        },\\n        \\\"T18_informationAsymmetry\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 10,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"kaelithKnows\\\": \\\"Lirien is carrying unresolved 'variables.' Lirien wants a future (Vael Seren). Bond synchronization enables combat survival.\\\",\\n                \\\"kaelithDoesNotKnow\\\": \\\"The kill contract. The loophole plan. The specific nature of Lirien's guilt.\\\",\\n                \\\"readerKnows\\\": \\\"Everything Kaelith knows PLUS: the kill contract details, the loophole mechanism, Lirien's guilt, Lirien's plan to stop Kaelith's heart.\\\",\\n                \\\"dramaticIrony\\\": \\\"Agonizing. 'Trust, offered freely, to someone who was using the silence to plan how to stop her heart.' Kaelith's 'someone I want tomorrows with' juxtaposed against Lirien's contract knowledge.\\\"\\n            }\\n        },\\n        \\\"T20_emotionalThroughline\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 10,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"progression\\\": \\\"fierce focus (combat) → terrified bond-dependency recognition → cautious surrender (intimacy) → guilty determination (loophole)\\\",\\n                \\\"startState\\\": \\\"Fierce focus — field-note precision, tactical awareness, bond as weapon.\\\",\\n                \\\"pivotMoment\\\": \\\"'She had surrendered control completely. And it had felt right.' — the operative who values control choosing to release it.\\\",\\n                \\\"endState\\\": \\\"Determined guilt — carrying both the loophole solution and the lie. Walking beside the woman she will save through the mechanism designed to kill her.\\\",\\n                \\\"matchesPlan\\\": True,\\n                \\\"noEmotionRepetitionFromCh13\\\": True\\n            }\\n        },\\n        \\\"T21_vulnerabilityLadder\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 10,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"step\\\": 5,\\n                \\\"moment\\\": \\\"Physical intimacy as surrender — first full intimate scene.\\\",\\n                \\\"earning\\\": \\\"Built on ch13 confession + first kiss. Combat proved interdependence. Intimacy explicitly chosen ('making a choice'), not bond-compelled, not survival-driven. Tactically worst conditions underscore deliberate choice.\\\",\\n                \\\"escalation\\\": \\\"Lirien surrenders control completely (operative who values control above all). Kaelith allows sounds to escape military discipline. Bond makes intimacy recursive — cannot hide during it. Genuine escalation from sharing unspeakable truths (ch13) to sharing bodies (ch14).\\\"\\n            }\\n        },\\n        \\\"T23_mysteryBoxInventory\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 9,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"MB-008_status\\\": \\\"Advanced from 'open' to 'partially answered' — loophole mechanism discovered but execution untested.\\\",\\n                \\\"activeCountPostCh14\\\": 12,\\n                \\\"targetRange\\\": \\\"3-7 (exceeded, but acceptable per story notes — conspiracy-heavy dual-arc structure)\\\",\\n                \\\"newBoxes\\\": \\\"None opened (appropriate).\\\",\\n                \\\"closedBoxes\\\": \\\"None closed (appropriate — MB-006 was closed in ch13).\\\"\\n            }\\n        },\\n        \\\"T24_subtextInDialogue\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 10,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"exchanges\\\": [\\n                    \\\"'Two down, one bound, the runner's secured.' — Surface: status report. Subtext: cover for fingers lingering on warm skin.\\\",\\n                    \\\"'I felt you take the echo.' — Surface: observing bond pain-sharing. Subtext: 'your pain is mine, and that matters to me.'\\\",\\n                    \\\"'Minor.' / 'I know.' — Surface: injury assessment. Subtext: 'I still need to touch it, and this need is not about medicine.'\\\",\\n                    \\\"'Inside.' — Surface: unclear referent. Subtext: 'come closer, I don't want the space between us.'\\\",\\n                    \\\"Vael Seren story — Surface: anecdote about a harbour. Subtext: 'I want a future with you but can't say it directly.'\\\",\\n                    \\\"'There are variables I haven't resolved.' — Surface: vague acknowledgment. Subtext: the kill contract.\\\",\\n                    \\\"'About solutions.' — Surface: problem-solving. Subtext: planning how to stop your heart to save your life.\\\"\\n                ],\\n                \\\"allChargedExchangesHaveSubtext\\\": True\\n            }\\n        },\\n        \\\"T25_thematicArgumentScaffolding\\\": {\\n            \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n            \\\"score\\\": 9,\\n            \\\"evidence\\\": {\\n                \\\"TP1_trust\\\": \\\"Combat requires absolute bond-enabled trust — survival depends on mutual vulnerability. Kaelith choosing not to demand the inventory tests whether trust can exist without full information. Theme embodied through action (combat synchronization) and choice (not pressing for secrets), not stated in narration.\\\",\\n                \\\"TP2_rightChoice\\\": \\\"Lirien's decision to hide the contract and seek the loophole is framed as 'the right choice' — protecting Kaelith from despair — but it is also a lie that will detonate. Tests the Act 2 'easy answer': can you solve moral problems with clever contractual logic?\\\",\\n                \\\"TP3_chosenVsOnly\\\": \\\"Intimacy explicitly chosen in tactically worst conditions. 'Making a choice' — not bond-compelled. But the contract underlying everything makes 'choice' questionable, testing the theme rather than simply affirming it.\\\",\\n                \\\"themeEmbodiedNotStated\\\": \\\"One borderline instance: 'a woman whose life had taught her that trust was the structural failure that preceded collapse' — character interpretation through Lirien's analytical lens, not authorial narration. Acceptable.\\\"\\n            }\\n        }\\n    },\\n    \\\"proseQualityFloor\\\": {\\n        \\\"cliches\\\": {\\\"count\\\": 0, \\\"max\\\": 2, \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\"},\\n        \\\"adverbsPerPage\\\": {\\\"count\\\": 1.5, \\\"max\\\": 3, \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\"},\\n        \\\"showTellRatio\\\": {\\\"estimated\\\": \\\"93:7\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"90:10\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\"},\\n        \\\"bannedPhrases\\\": {\\\"count\\\": 0, \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\", \\\"note\\\": \\\"'suddenly' removed in correction\\\"},\\n        \\\"metaphorDomains\\\": {\\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\", \\\"note\\\": \\\"All metaphors from Lirien's domains: water, currents, surfaces, contract logic, operational precision\\\"},\\n        \\\"dialogueWithoutBeat\\\": {\\\"max\\\": 6, \\\"limit\\\": 6, \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS (at limit)\\\"},\\n        \\\"consecutiveReflectiveParagraphs\\\": {\\\"max\\\": 3, \\\"limit\\\": 2, \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASS (improved from 12 to 3 with corrections; remaining 3 are short transition paragraphs in combat)\\\"},\\n        \\\"modernSlang\\\": {\\\"count\\\": 0, \\\"status